      summary: String.raw`Independence is defined for σ-fields and checked on π-systems, which lets the chapter build independent sequences, compute laws of sums by convolution and construct infinite product spaces. Weak laws come from second-moment estimates and truncation; the Borel–Cantelli lemmas turn summability into almost-sure statements and lead to Etemadi's strong law. The optional sections treat random series (Kolmogorov's 0-1 law, maximal inequality, three-series theorem), renewal theory and Cramér's large deviations.`,
